     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":3,\"rationale\":\"The target is an OR of three parents, so all three must be cut.\\n\\n1. h4_1:reach is fed only by h2_2:access, which comes from edge1. Blocking one step (h4_1 or h2_2) cuts this branch, at a cost of 1.\\n\\n2. h4_2:access (OR of h2_1 and h3_1) and h4_0:obtain (AND of h3_2, h3_1 and h2_0) cannot both be cut by a single block:\\n- h2_1 depends only on h1_2.\\n- h3_1 depends only on h2_3.\\n- Blocking h3_1 kills h4_0, but h4_2 survives via h2_1.\\n- Blocking h1_2 kills h2_1 and h2_0 (so h4_0), but h4_2 survives via h3_1.\\n- Blocking h2_3 kills h4_0, but h4_2 survives via h2_1.\\nSo this pair needs 2 blocks, e.g. {h4_2, h4_0} or {h2_1, h3_1}.\\n\\nTotal minimum is 3, for example {h4_1, h4_2, h4_0}.\"}"
    }
